!  Grid convergence, measured 2026-08-12 (BLYP/cc-pVDZ). NOTE the table below
!  was taken with pruning_scheme= jayatilaka2, which this job used to request
!  and which was REMOVED on 2026-08-14 for being too rough (-1.5e-5 against g09
!  on an open-shell case, where every other scheme was within 1.6e-6). The
!  convergence PATTERN still holds, but the absolute numbers were re-blessed on
!  the default treutler_ahlrichs grid -- see the stdout reference.
!  Until then this block had NO effect at all: MOLECULE.SET:initialize_DFT_grids
!  destroyed and recreated the BECKE_GRID, so every DFT run silently used the
!  type defaults while put_basics echoed back whatever was asked for. All seven
!  accuracies gave a bit-identical -76.400240454361 in an unchanging 0.8 s.
!  With that fixed:
!
!     accuracy     total energy        vs "best"     time
!     very_low     -76.398747906904    +1.5e-3       0.34 s
!     low          -76.400242979280    -1.5e-5       0.46 s
!     medium       -76.400217194173    +1.1e-5       0.75 s
!     high         -76.400224312693    +3.9e-6       1.15 s
!     very_high    -76.400219647629    +8.6e-6       2.24 s
!     extreme      -76.400227655128    +5.9e-7       4.53 s
!     best         -76.400228241093     --           8.72 s
!
!  Convergence is not monotonic -- quadrature error oscillates, it is not
!  variational in the grid -- so "closer to converged" must be read from the
!  magnitude, not the sign. very_low is unusable (1.5e-3). Everything from
!  low upward sits within ~1.5e-5 of the converged -76.4002282, so "low" is
!  kept: it is the cheapest setting that is converged to well beyond what this
!  test needs, and this is a "short" test.

   becke_grid = {
      set_defaults
      accuracy= low
      put_basics
   }


   scfdata= {

      initial_density= promolecule
    ! initial_density= core
    ! initial_mos= unrestricted
    ! initial_mos= restricted

    ! kind=            uks
      kind=            rks

      dft_exchange_functional= becke88
      dft_correlation_functional= lyp

      direct=          on

      convergence= 0.00001

      diis= { convergence_tolerance= 0.00001 }

      output= NO
      output_results= YES

   }
   
   scf

   delete_scf_archives

}

